PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
- Consensus remains unanimous across all colleagues for Option B (increase, more, Keap1).
- (2E)-4-Hydroxy-2-nonen-8-ynal activates Nrf2 to transcriptionally increase ALDH levels, while 50 µM 4-OI produces a more pronounced induction due to efficient Keap1 alkylation without the proteotoxicity of reactive aldehydes.
- Keap1 is the established cysteine-based electrophile sensor mediating this cytoprotective pathway.
- Final choice B is locked with no dissenting views.
}

